  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Only one man holds the key to this door.",
      "shot": 0,
      "at": 0.25,
      "seconds": 3.15
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Each Sunday, two kinsmen walked London in silence.",
      "shot": 1,
      "at": 4.417,
      "seconds": 4.58
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Utterson drank gin alone, yet ruined men found in him their last friend.",
      "shot": 2,
      "at": 9.917,
      "seconds": 5.18
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "Did you ever remark that door? It holds a very odd story.",
      "shot": 3,
      "at": 15.917,
      "seconds": 4.45
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "gabriel_john_utterson",
      "text": "Indeed? And what was that?",
      "shot": 4,
      "at": 21.292,
      "seconds": 2.03
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "tale",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "Three o'clock of a black winter morning, street after street lit, and empty as a church.",
      "shot": 6,
      "at": 28.792,
      "seconds": 5.89
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "tale",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "They ran into one another.",
      "shot": 7,
      "at": 35.583,
      "seconds": 1.73
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "tale",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "And the man trampled calmly over the child's body and left her screaming on the ground.",
      "shot": 8,
      "at": 38.25,
      "seconds": 5.14
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "tale",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "I collared my gentleman. He gave me one look, so ugly it brought out the sweat on me.",
      "shot": 9,
      "at": 44.708,
      "seconds": 6.58
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "tale",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "We swore to make his name stink from one end of London to the other.",
      "shot": 10,
      "at": 51.917,
      "seconds": 4.48
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "edward_hyde",
      "text": "No gentleman but wishes to avoid a scene. Name your figure.",
      "shot": 11,
      "at": 57.333,
      "seconds": 4.42
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "kind": "tale",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "Gold, and a cheque.",
      "shot": 12,
      "at": 62.667,
      "seconds": 1.84
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Next morning the bank paid the cheque. Enfield named the place Black Mail House.",
      "shot": 13,
      "at": 66.333,
      "seconds": 7.34
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "kind": "inner",
      "speaker": "gabriel_john_utterson",
      "text": "Who signed it? Does he live there?",
      "shot": 14,
      "at": 74.292,
      "seconds": 2.29
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Enfield kept one rule: the more a thing looked like Queer Street, the less he asked.",
      "shot": 15,
      "at": 77.5,
      "seconds": 6.04
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "They walked on; Utterson weighed the tale.",
      "shot": 18,
      "at": 88.542,
      "seconds": 4.25
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "gabriel_john_utterson",
      "text": "I want to ask the name of that man who walked over the child.",
      "shot": 19,
      "at": 93.792,
      "seconds": 3.84
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "It was a man of the name of Hyde.",
      "shot": 20,
      "at": 98.542,
      "seconds": 2.79
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "gabriel_john_utterson",
      "text": "I do not ask the other party's name. I know it already.",
      "shot": 22,
      "at": 106.792,
      "seconds": 3.98
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "richard_enfield",
      "text": "He has the key still. I saw him use it not a week ago.",
      "shot": 23,
      "at": 112.417,
      "seconds": 3.9
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "gabriel_john_utterson",
      "text": "With all my heart, Richard.",
      "shot": 25,
      "at": 120.75,
      "seconds": 1.89
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "The door kept its secret; Hyde kept the key.",
      "shot": 27,
      "at": 128.167,
      "seconds": 3.61
    }
  ],
  "plan": "e61ea2f7c0855ac6"
}